Period bloating is usually temporary, but persistent or severe abdominal swelling should not automatically be assumed to be caused by menstruation. If bloating is severe, continues well beyond your period, or is associated with significant pain or other unusual symptoms, speak with a healthcare professional.

Understanding your menstrual symptoms can help you identify what is normal for your body. Tracking symptoms across several cycles may help you recognise patterns.

Overall, gentle movement, hydration, balanced meals, adequate sleep, and suitable menstrual products can support greater comfort during your period.
